edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186511486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157425 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186511545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157425 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157425 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186157002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157425 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157481 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157481 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157481 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157481 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157481 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157481 #edb/ref 1045 "The Second Derivative of a Multivariable Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157481 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186158351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157481 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157481 #edb/ref 1050 660.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157481 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "980e0bea-1189-578f-9781-512b76215027" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158351 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158351 #edb/ref 1061 45105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158351 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bac39a49-196c-50bd-99ec-d3c5b74be977" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158351 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186158568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158352 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158352 #edb/ref 1061 45106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158352 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bdf28805-f615-5f91-bade-c3cb7038cfd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158352 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158353 #edb/ref 1061 45109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158353 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e732cfd5-6c10-55ef-b698-a932a1d233c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158353 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158354 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158354 #edb/ref 1061 45116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158354 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8222059e-dad9-55b4-8e1d-ac327c86df18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158354 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158568 #edb/ref 1064 "We've seen how to calculate the total derivative of a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R.$ In this lesson, we will learn how to calculate its second derivative.\n\nFor a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n\n![](images/44/44a95860d7e7bd926f4d94c2ebb5b037e8537ac622f7c86b500aa06b9f959250.svg)\n\nthe total derivative of $f$ is given by the matrix\n\n![](images/e0/e0c9f72b67a531f992342e9f9e0b74f447de5e2b62c9fd81f08804096a912e67.svg)\n\nTo differentiate $f$ once more, we first need to take the transpose of the first derivative:\n\n![](images/4d/4d23282171c39149eeebd7301550ebdf1727b86736a57de6e5d7b6ea96891157.svg)\n\nTo calculate the **second derivative** of $f,$ we simply apply the definition of the total derivative to $\\left(\\boldsymbol f'(\\mathbf x)\\right)^T.$ By doing this, we get the following $n\\times n$ matrix:\n\n![](images/3d/3d62db0c4018fcce47077285aa05e6c4ea3c79e972ab87fccf5165a07083eda9.svg)\n\nNotice that this matrix is *symmetric* due to the equality of mixed partial derivatives. This becomes important later. \n\nThe matrix $\\boldsymbol{f}''(\\mathbf x)$ is sometimes called the **Hessian matrix,** and its determinant, \n\n$$\nH(\\mathbf x) = \\det\\big( \\boldsymbol{f}''(\\mathbf x) \\big)\n$$\n\nis called the **Hessian determinant**.\n\nNote that in the case of a two-variable function $f(x,y),$ the second derivative is given by\n\n![](images/e8/e83195902ce2cdc2e0ff6c1f51ebc679a4bddd51fedd38c4bc6fddc4c73373dd.svg)\n\nIn this lesson, we'll primarily focus on two-variable functions $f(x,y).$ However, we should remember that the techniques discussed here can be applied to scalar functions with an arbitrary number of variables." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158568 #edb/ref 1065 7795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158568 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "79cc27de-f461-55d9-ab0f-3dd5a21dd4f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158568 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236443 #edb/ref 1080 "-{\\pi }^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236443 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236443 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "62d58fc9-233d-5a98-9f47-8a3790a441f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236615 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236615 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236615 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "804c671d-3217-5280-aa02-fe2a73812ecc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236672 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236672 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236672 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88c43743-4bdd-5d6d-8482-949f26f0705c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236758 #edb/ref 1080 "1-2{\\pi }^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236758 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236758 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "944e0f31-80d6-5eac-8960-7ada905bec43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237192 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\pi }^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237192 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237192 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d93bce69-5901-5324-bd97-83116ddf04a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237601 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237601 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237601 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237601 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237601 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186237192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237601 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237601 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237601 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186236672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237601 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "77c1b5e6-8017-5a27-ad73-0d376c902134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281784 #edb/ref 1080 "32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281784 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281784 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a7ccfc6-c980-5f87-98b3-cb27c26de86d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281949 #edb/ref 1080 "-40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281949 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281949 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1cc546d0-b0b6-5368-af23-5ec0c2c96352" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282301 #edb/ref 1080 "-16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282301 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282301 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "48389a8d-c104-542e-8686-3b973c39c4df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282783 #edb/ref 1080 "-28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282783 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282783 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7f03e21b-fba2-5b1e-bbaa-ba00d1112786" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283391 #edb/ref 1080 "25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283391 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283391 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c372c923-e6e7-5ef4-8346-000c6e272e18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284069 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186281784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284069 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186281949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284069 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186282301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284069 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186282783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284069 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186283391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284069 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284069 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284069 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186282783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284069 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "533cc9b6-1b67-5a24-ae39-2f81ecaf9c2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284390 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284390 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163642" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284390 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284390 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}4xy-3{y}^{2} & 2{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{bmatrix},$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186284390 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "64116d30-10df-5392-b872-327ec4131913" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284390 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det(\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n$\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}4xy-3{y}^{2} & 2{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{bmatrix},$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=4xy-3{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}-6xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy-3{y}^{2})=4y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-6xy)=4x-6y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy-3{y}^{2})=4x-6y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-6xy)=-6x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4y & 4x-6y \\\\ 4x-6y & -6x\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{″}(1,1)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=4\\cdot (-6)-(-2)\\cdot (-2)=-28.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348479 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}2y & 2x \\\\ 2x & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348479 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348479 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0379a8f3-5c08-5a0e-9aa9-ee7247f5bb7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348580 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}2y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348580 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348580 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0f2c18f5-f6c6-5cb7-9bd3-ef891a719882" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348671 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348671 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348671 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1a863fee-48cb-518a-94c7-332f0d5dfb90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348748 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}2y & 2xy \\\\ 2xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348748 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348748 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "235323a0-a480-5c75-9639-2308eb39664a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348749 #edb/ref 1080 "-8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348749 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348749 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "236352e1-e284-5137-93e8-01d0c0b82dd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348915 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2y \\\\ 2y & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186348915 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348915 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3438c329-ab2c-5701-840d-707e4cfa738f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349481 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186349481 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349481 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "703d071f-0017-59ad-ade4-9601ec2c639e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350254 #edb/ref 1080 "14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350254 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350254 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cd6da9cd-0b80-5391-a066-ff87ff441cbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350322 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350322 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350322 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d5b5d5ad-403a-5e9b-b47e-9495ed54eecd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350365 #edb/ref 1080 "-12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350365 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350365 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "da828216-6cb2-53d2-9a0c-74a4b4c5a870" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186350254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186350322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186350365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350734 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350734 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350734 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186350365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350734 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0f56bbbf-1a13-5c6d-a2d7-69c5469daa32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186349481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350749 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350749 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350749 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186349481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350749 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1892be87-58b9-5f45-a8a1-451663b051c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351229 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351229 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81119" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351229 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351229 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)={y}^{2}({x}^{2}-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351229 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "235e87ab-40f0-5bca-9e1d-4479ce5e2de8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351229 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}({x}^{2}-1)) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}({x}^{2}-1))\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2x{y}^{2} & 2y({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y({x}^{2}-1))=4xy \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2})=4xy\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y({x}^{2}-1))=2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186394105 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186394106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394105 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80947" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394105 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394105 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394105 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b55b18c-139d-56b5-94eb-26aeb293ef39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394105 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy}) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}y{e}^{xy} & x{e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{xy})={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{xy})={e}^{xy}+xy\\,\\text{ }{e}^{xy} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})={e}^{xy}+xy\\,\\text{ }{e}^{xy}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{xy})={x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(1+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(1+xy) & {x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186394106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394111 #edb/ref