2186430443 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430443 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186430423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430443 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eca99a2b-d50a-519b-aef0-e2b86f3c4cf7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430445 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430445 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102461" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430445 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430445 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430445 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "98de8580-5081-5c82-af81-6826d2545a45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430445 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & \\frac{x}{y}-1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}-1)=\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}-1)=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1045 "The Second Derivative of a Multivariable Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186481451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "0d220057-0079-57e6-bb5c-eb3461a91e72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480829 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186480829 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480829 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2fca28ad-f59e-5a0a-bb4c-0662386d1e94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480831 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186480831 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480831 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3075a971-db98-5b66-a3d1-9af12fdf